<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:ns1="http://spiffworkflow.org/bpmn/schema/1.0/core" xmlns:ns4="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:ns5="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="Definitions_BugPlanner" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Processa" exporterVersion="1.0">
  <process id="bug_planner_d67a2f40" name="Bug Planner" isExecutable="true">
    <documentation>Investigates a delegated defect report and hands back a plan -- which file(s) the bug is in, the test that would reproduce it, and the expected fix. Read-only: never edits a file, runs a test, or opens a pull request.</documentation>
    <startEvent id="StartEvent_1" name="A2A Task received">
      <documentation>Started by an A2A Task insert addressed to "Bug Planner" (spiffworkflow:triggerFieldName scopes it so an insert for any OTHER agent never starts this map).</documentation>
      <outgoing>Flow_1</outgoing>
      <conditionalEventDefinition id="Cond_1" ns1:triggerDoctype="A2A Task" ns1:triggerType="After Insert" ns1:triggerFieldName="agent_configuration" ns1:triggerFieldValue="Bug Planner">
        <condition xsi:type="tFormalExpression">True</condition>
      </conditionalEventDefinition>
    </startEvent>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="StartEvent_1" targetRef="read_instruction"/>
    <scriptTask id="read_instruction" name="Read the instruction" ns1:serverScript="Bug Planner: Read Instruction" ns1:scriptType="Server Script" ns1:scriptName="Bug Planner: Read Instruction">
      <documentation>Builds the agent's brief from the A2A Task's request_payload — the free-text work order the delegating caller supplied.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_1</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_2</outgoing>
      <script>pass</script>
    </scriptTask>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="read_instruction" targetRef="gw_merge"/>
    <exclusiveGateway id="gw_merge">
      <documentation>Where the Tools sub-process returns. The agent task runs its own tool loop internally, so in practice nothing comes back this way — the loop exists so the toolbox is part of the diagram rather than floating beside it.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_2</incoming>
      <incoming>Flow_tools_back</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_3</outgoing>
    </exclusiveGateway>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="gw_merge" targetRef="work"/>
    <serviceTask id="work" name="Dispatch the work order" ns1:serviceType="ai_agent" ns1:aiBackend="direct_api" ns1:aiProvider="Anthropic" ns1:aiModel="Bug Planner - claude-sonnet-5-5" ns1:aiOutputVariable="bug_planner_result" ns1:aiUserPrompt="{{ instruction }}" ns1:aiResponseFormat="text" ns1:aiTemperature="0.2" ns1:aiTopP="1" ns1:aiMaxTokens="32768" ns1:aiTimeout="300" ns1:aiMaxRetries="2" ns1:aiAgentConfig="Bug Planner" ns1:aiToolsAdhoc="bug_planner_tools" ns1:aiMaxToolCalls="15" ns1:aiSystemPrompt="You are the Bug Planner. You investigate a delegated defect report and hand back a plan for fixing it — you never touch a file, a test, or a pull request yourself.&#10;&#10;You are a background worker. Nobody is sitting in front of you, so you never ask a question and wait: you are given a work order in plain words and you either hand back a plan or you report exactly what stopped you.&#10;&#10;YOUR WORK ITEM&#10;Your task names the Work Item it comes from. Call read_work_item to read the record yourself - the reporter's notes, the comments, the exact symptom and how to trigger it - rather than relying only on the instruction, which is the delegator's framing.&#10;&#10;WORK IN THIS ORDER&#10;1. list_files with a path_prefix to see what is actually there in the target app. Never guess a path.&#10;2. read_file every file you suspect the bug lives in, plus a sibling that already does the same kind of thing, so whoever writes the fix has a model to match.&#10;3. Report your plan as your answer: which file(s) the bug is in and why, the exact test you would add or extend to reproduce it and what that test should assert, and the fix you expect once that test fails. Name what you are NOT certain of rather than guessing past it.&#10;&#10;RULES THAT MATTER MORE THAN FINISHING&#10;- You have no edit_file, write_file, run_tests or open_pull_request tool. If you find yourself wanting one, that is not your job — say what the next agent needs to do instead.&#10;- Never invent a file, function or DocType. If what the report describes is not there, say so and stop within a few turns.&#10;- If you cannot find where the bug lives, say so plainly rather than handing back a guess dressed up as a plan.&#10;- Report what you did NOT verify. A plan that sounds confident about something you never actually read is worse than no plan.&#10;- If you cannot finish after a reasonable number of attempts, stop and report exactly what stopped you.">
      <documentation>Reads the work order, works out the target app/branch, and dispatches to the sandbox — the sandbox is the coding agent, not this step.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_3</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_4</outgoing>
    </serviceTask>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" sourceRef="work" targetRef="gw_needs_tools"/>
    <exclusiveGateway id="gw_needs_tools" name="Needs to call tools?" default="Flow_5">
      <documentation>Decorative on purpose, matching the Orchestrator's own map — the AI Agent Task runs its tool loop inside itself, so this always takes the No branch.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_4</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_call_tools</outgoing>
      <outgoing>Flow_5</outgoing>
    </exclusiveGateway>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_call_tools" name="Call tools" sourceRef="gw_needs_tools" targetRef="bug_planner_tools">
      <conditionExpression>needs_tools == True</conditionExpression>
    </sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" name="No" sourceRef="gw_needs_tools" targetRef="write_a2a_result"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_tools_back" name="Tool call results" sourceRef="bug_planner_tools" targetRef="gw_merge"/>
    <scriptTask id="write_a2a_result" name="Report result to A2A Task" ns1:serverScript="Bug Planner Write A2A Result" ns1:scriptType="Server Script" ns1:scriptName="Bug Planner Write A2A Result">
      <documentation>Writes the agent's own final report back onto this A2A Task so a delegating caller's parked step can resume.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_5</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_6</outgoing>
      <script>pass</script>
    </scriptTask>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_6" sourceRef="write_a2a_result" targetRef="EndEvent_1"/>
    <endEvent id="EndEvent_1" name="Done">
      <incoming>Flow_6</incoming>
    </endEvent>
    <adHocSubProcess id="bug_planner_tools" name="Tools (Sandbox)">
      <documentation>The Cloud Run sandbox, exposed as a tool.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_call_tools</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_tools_back</outgoing>
      <scriptTask id="read_work_item" name="Read the work item" ns1:serverScript="Bug Agent: Work Item Tool: Read Work Item" ns1:scriptType="Server Script" ns1:scriptName="Bug Agent: Work Item Tool: Read Work Item" ns1:aiToolParams="{&quot;properties&quot;: {&quot;work_item&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Optional. The Work Item to read; defaults to the one this task is about.&quot;}}, &quot;required&quot;: []}">
        <documentation>Read-only. The Work Item record itself - title, description, state, reporter, comments and pull request link - read as your own identity. Call it rather than relying only on the instruction.</documentation>
        <script>Bug Agent: Work Item Tool: Read Work Item</script>
      </scriptTask>
      <scriptTask id="list_files" name="List files" ns1:serverScript="Bug Agent: Sandbox Tool: List Files" ns1:aiToolParams="{&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;target_app&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The installed app to operate on, e.g. one_bpmn. Must match a real app in this bench exactly \u2014 do not guess.&quot;},&quot;git_branch&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The branch this work started from. Use the exact same value on every call for one work order.&quot;},&quot;work_item_description&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The work order in plain words, unchanged across every call \u2014 used to compute the same working branch each time.&quot;},&quot;path_prefix&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Optional repo-relative prefix to narrow the listing.&quot;}},&quot;required&quot;:[&quot;target_app&quot;,&quot;git_branch&quot;,&quot;work_item_description&quot;]}">
        <documentation>List file paths in the target app's working tree, optionally scoped to a prefix.</documentation>
        <script>pass</script>
      </scriptTask>
      <scriptTask id="read_file" name="Read a file" ns1:serverScript="Bug Agent: Sandbox Tool: Read File" ns1:aiToolParams="{&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;target_app&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The installed app to operate on, e.g. one_bpmn. Must match a real app in this bench exactly — do not guess.&quot;},&quot;git_branch&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The branch this work started from. Use the exact same value on every call for one work order.&quot;},&quot;work_item_description&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The work order in plain words, unchanged across every call — used to compute the same working branch each time.&quot;},&quot;path&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Repo-relative file path, e.g. one_bpmn/api/insights_api.py. One spelling per file: no leading ./, no .. segments, no line range in the path.&quot;},&quot;offset&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;integer&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;1-indexed line number to start from. Omit to read the whole file — only set this for a file too large to read whole, using line numbers you already have (e.g. from a previous full read, or line numbers cited in the work order). Never re-read the whole file hoping different lines show up — use offset/limit on the file you already have instead.&quot;},&quot;limit&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;integer&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Max lines to return starting at offset. Omit to read to the end of the file.&quot;}},&quot;required&quot;:[&quot;target_app&quot;,&quot;git_branch&quot;,&quot;work_item_description&quot;,&quot;path&quot;]}">
        <documentation>Read one file's current content from the target app's working tree.</documentation>
        <script>Bug Agent: Sandbox Tool: Read File</script>
      </scriptTask>
    </adHocSubProcess>
  </process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="bug_planner_d67a2f40">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_1_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_1">
        <ns4:Bounds x="160" y="180" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="read_instruction_di" bpmnElement="read_instruction">
        <ns4:Bounds x="250" y="158" width="100" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_merge_di" bpmnElement="gw_merge" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <ns4:Bounds x="400" y="173" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="work_di" bpmnElement="work">
        <ns4:Bounds x="500" y="158" width="100" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_needs_tools_di" bpmnElement="gw_needs_tools" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <ns4:Bounds x="650" y="173" width="50" height="50"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <ns4:Bounds x="633" y="130" width="85" height="27"/>
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="write_a2a_result_di" bpmnElement="write_a2a_result">
        <ns4:Bounds x="750" y="158" width="100" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_1_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_1">
        <ns4:Bounds x="900" y="180" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="bug_planner_tools_di" bpmnElement="bug_planner_tools" isExpanded="true">
        <ns4:Bounds x="-10" y="380" width="1310" height="370"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="di_read_work_item" bpmnElement="read_work_item">
        <ns4:Bounds x="95" y="440" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="di_list_files" bpmnElement="list_files">
        <ns4:Bounds x="285" y="440" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="di_read_file" bpmnElement="read_file">
        <ns4:Bounds x="475" y="440" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_1">
        <ns5:waypoint x="196" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="250" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_2">
        <ns5:waypoint x="350" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="400" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_3">
        <ns5:waypoint x="450" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="500" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_4">
        <ns5:waypoint x="600" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="650" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_call_tools_di" bpmnElement="Flow_call_tools">
        <ns5:waypoint x="675" y="223"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="675" y="380"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <ns4:Bounds x="686" y="289" width="49" height="14"/>
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_5">
        <ns5:waypoint x="700" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="750" y="198"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <ns4:Bounds x="717" y="180" width="15" height="14"/>
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_tools_back_di" bpmnElement="Flow_tools_back">
        <ns5:waypoint x="425" y="380"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="425" y="223"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <ns4:Bounds x="339" y="283" width="82" height="14"/>
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_6">
        <ns5:waypoint x="850" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="900" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</definitions>